Below is a quick summary of what’s happening and the minimal change needed to prevent NaN coordinates from ever being returned in the auto-placement util.

1) Bug summary and root cause  
   - When you delete the only start event on an empty diagram and then add a Group, that Group is treated by the “auto-place” logic as a normal shape but never really gets proper `width`/`height` assigned.  
   - The next time you auto-place another shape (e.g. a Pool/Participant) “to the right” of that Group, the code runs  
       x = sourceTrbl.right + DEFAULT_HORIZONTAL_DISTANCE + element.width/2  
     but `element.width` is `undefined` (or non-finite), so you end up with `NaN`.  
   - Downstream, the SVG transform call `setTranslate(NaN, …)` blows up.  

2) Patch  
   We simply ensure that whenever we do `… + element.width/2` we first coerce `element.width` to a usable number (fallback to 0). The only method that really needs this guard is `getDefaultPosition` (all other positioning routines only run when they have a very specific shape type and will have real numbers).  

